      "note": "False positive. `Open3.capture3(*args)` is invoked with an ARGV ARRAY, so Ruby execs the binary directly with NO shell \u2014 there is no shell-injection vector. `F3D` is an operator-controlled constant (ENV['F3D_BIN'] default 'f3d'); the input/output paths are Tempfile-generated, not user-supplied; and `size` is an integer preview dimension passed as its own argv element (a malformed value would just make f3d error out, which is handled). No user input reaches a shell."
