      "user_input": "exts.size",
      "confidence": "Weak",
      "cwe_id": [
        89
      ],
      "note": "False positive, and Brakeman's own `user_input` field says so: the flagged interpolation is `exts.size`, an INTEGER COUNT, not a value. The clause is `Array.new(exts.size, LIKE_EXT).join(\" OR \")` where LIKE_EXT is a frozen constant, so what varies with user input is only HOW MANY TIMES a fixed string is repeated -- Brakeman renders that join as `#{exts.size}` and flags the interpolation. Every extension travels as a BOUND parameter (`*exts.map { like_pattern(e) }`), never into the SQL text. Two independent layers stand behind that anyway: `resolve_exts` drops anything not matching /\\A[a-z0-9]{1,8}\\z/ and caps the list at MAX_EXTS (so `exts.size` is 1..8 and every element is alphanumeric), and `like_pattern` runs `sanitize_sql_like` with an explicit ESCAPE clause. Driven directly with `%`, `_`, `../`, over-length and array-shaped params -- all dropped before the query is built."
    }
